;; repr/asm's arm64 encode check's classes (bin/repr-asm --arch arm64 encode-check; doc/asm/SPEC.md §12; doc/asm/ARM64-SURVEY.md,
;; "As built: AR2 (first slice)"): every line of test/asm/encode-results-arm64.edn that does not pass at a level (:level, both when
;; left out) is in the first class whose :match finds its REASON (or whose :ids names it), in goi's format. A `mismatch:` (a word
;; that differs from the stated one) or a `crash:` is in no class: it fails the check. Read with the Clojure reader.
[
 {:id :extension
  :level :encode
  :title "an instruction beyond arm64asm's table (ARMv8.0's base A64, FP and NEON)"
  :kind :deferred
  :why "the table is golang.org/x/arch/arm64/arm64asm's (ARS5 (a)), which holds ARMv8.0: the later extensions' mnemonics (LSE's atomics, RCPC, PAuth, BTI, MTE, the dot products, FHM, complex numbers, MOPS, CSSC's new mnemonics, the 128-bit system instructions, Apple's AMX-free extensions ...) are AR2's next slices, from Go's cmd/internal/obj/arm64 optab or Arm's specification after its licence (ARS24)"
  :decided "ARS5 (a) (the user, 2026-11-09): Go's tables and arm64asm first"
  :match [#"^no-mnemonic: "]}
 {:id :sysreg-name
  :level :encode
  :title "a system register or PSTATE field Go's tables do not name"
  :kind :deferred
  :why "MRS and MSR name their register from cmd/internal/obj/arm64's sysRegEnc.go (431 registers, the ARMv8.0-8.5 ones Go's assembler knows) or the generic S<op0>_<op1>_C<n>_C<m>_<op2>; LLVM's tests name about 930 more (Armv8-R's, the trace unit's, GICv3's, the debug and PMU extensions', ...) and the later PSTATE fields (PAN, UAO, DIT, TCO, ...): their encodings need a register table (ARS24)"
  :decided "ARS5 (a); ARS24 proposes the table"
  :match [#"^operands: (mrs|msr) "]}
 {:id :sysop-name
  :level :encode
  :title "a system instruction's operation Go's tables do not name"
  :kind :deferred
  :why "AT, DC, IC and TLBI name their operation from arm64asm's sysInstsAttrs (the ARMv8.0 TLBI and DC ones); AT's and IC's are not in it, nor the later TLBI and DC operations (outer shareable, range, nXS, MTE's DC ...)"
  :decided "ARS5 (a); ARS24"
  :match [#"^operands: (tlbi|at|dc|ic) "]}
 {:id :fp16
  :level :encode
  :title "half-precision floating point (FEAT_FP16, ARMv8.2)"
  :kind :deferred
  :why "arm64asm's FP and NEON rows have no H-register or 4H/8H floating-point forms: the FP16 extension's encodings are an extension's (:extension's source)"
  :decided "ARS5 (a); ARS24"
  :match [#"^operands: (f[a-z0-9]*|[su]cvtf)(\.[48]h |\.h | .*(\bh[0-9]+\b|\.[48]h\b|\.h\[))"]}
 {:id :extension-operands
  :level :encode
  :title "a later extension's operands on a base mnemonic"
  :kind :deferred
  :why "the mnemonic is ARMv8.0's but these operands are a later extension's: CSSC's SMIN/SMAX/UMIN/UMAX/ABS/CNT/CTZ on general registers (ARMv8.9), RCPC3's pre-indexed STLR, the PRFM SLC targets, DSB's nXS options (ARMv8.7)"
  :decided "ARS5 (a); ARS24"
  :match [#"^operands: ([su](min|max)|abs|cnt|ctz) [wx]" #"^operands: stlr .*!$" #"^operands: prfm p..slc" #"^operands: dsb [a-z]*nxs"]}
 {:id :check-text
  :title "a CHECK line whose text is not one instruction's"
  :kind :design
  :why "the line states its encoding after a text that is not the instruction's: a part of it (`CHECK: sp, x3, x7, lsl #4` after `CHECK: sub` on the line before), a FileCheck regular expression beyond alternatives, classes and optional groups (`#{{1.06250*(e\\+00)?}}`), or no text where the instructions before the block are not as many as its lines"
  :decided "AR2's judge reads a CHECK text, an alternative of it, or the input line a text-less block pairs with"
  :match [#"^read: no CHECK text" #"^read: unexpected , " #"^read: invalid character \"\?\""]}
 {:id :directive
  :level :encode
  :title "a directive's bytes"
  :kind :design
  :why "`.tlsdesccall var` states an empty encoding and a relocation: a directive's bytes and relocations are the object writer's (AR4), not the instruction encoder's"
  :decided "doc/asm/ARM64-SURVEY.md §12: AR4"
  :match [#"^directive: "]}
 {:id :print-radix
  :level :print
  :title "an immediate LLVM prints in hexadecimal"
  :kind :deferred
  :why "the canonical print writes integers in decimal (AR1's rule); LLVM's InstPrinter writes a logical immediate (AND, ORR, EOR, TST, MOV's ORR alias) and MOVI's 64-bit pattern in hexadecimal, which a print by the operand's class (the table's argument kind) gives: AR2's next slice (ARS25)"
  :decided "ARS25 proposes the class-aware print"
  :match [#"^print: .*\(stated: .*#0x"]}
 ;; the reject level: each `error:` line of an error test (its RUN lines run `not llvm-mc`) with the instruction it names
 {:id :message
  :level :reject
  :title "rejected, without LLVM's message"
  :kind :deferred
  :why "repr/asm refuses the instruction (its reader, no row of the table, no row taking the operands, an unpredictable form) but gives no message in LLVM's words, so the line's fragment is not met: the matcher's messages (AArch64AsmParser's diagnostics by operand class) are AR2's next slice"
  :decided "doc/asm/ARM64-SURVEY.md §12, AR2's exit: rejected with the fragment or classed :message"
  :match [#"^rejected: "]}
 {:id :feature-gate
  :level :reject
  :title "rejected by LLVM for a feature the test's RUN line leaves out"
  :kind :deferred
  :why "the error is `instruction requires: FEATURE` or a system register's (`expected readable system register`, `expected writable ...`) that the test's -mattr does not enable (the same instruction or register encodes in the test that enables it); the encoder takes no feature set yet: the -mattr features as data are AR2's next slice"
  :decided "AR2's first slice: no feature sets"
  :match [#"^accepted: .*requires: " #"^accepted: expected (writable|readable) system register"]}
 {:id :relocation
  :level :reject
  :title "a relocation's or an expression's error"
  :kind :deferred
  :why "the error is the object writer's or the expression evaluator's (a relocation the target does not support, COFF's specifiers, an addend out of range, an undefined symbol in a subtraction, an expression that is not relocatable, Apple's @PAGEOFF on ELF, a literal too large for its register): AR4's"
  :decided "doc/asm/ARM64-SURVEY.md §12: AR4"
  :match [#"^accepted: (relocation specifier|addend too big|symbol .* can not be undefined|expected relocatable expression|unexpected adr label|page or gotpage|invalid immediate expression|Immediate too large)"]}
 {:id :operand-spelling
  :level :reject
  :title "an operand spelling LLVM's matcher rejects and its printer writes"
  :kind :deferred
  :why "`add x2, x4, w2, uxtx`: LLVM's matcher wants an X register with UXTX and SXTX, but its printer writes the W register (`adds x1, x2, w3, uxtx` in arm64-arithmetic-encoding's CHECK lines), which the encoder reads; the input's stricter spelling is the matcher's (AR2's next slice)"
  :decided "AR2's first slice"
  :match [#"^accepted: expected '\[su\]xt\[bhw\]' with optional integer in range \[0, 4\] \| add x2, x4, w2, uxtx$"]}
 {:id :no-instruction
  :level :reject
  :title "an error line that names no instruction"
  :kind :design
  :why "the error line neither echoes an instruction nor follows one (a directive's error, a block of errors after a block of inputs, an error about the file): the reject level judges an instruction's rejection"
  :decided "AR2's judge"
  :match [#"^no-text: " #"^directive: "]}
]
